@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .
@prefix intake: <https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/intake/> .
@prefix mod: <https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/> .
@prefix owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix proc: <https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/> .
@prefix skos: <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .
@prefix src: <https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

proc:CM-1-1-1-1-1 a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:references [ a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
            dcterms:identifier "10252" ;
            dcterms:isPartOf src:apqc-pcf-7.2.2 ;
            dcterms:title "APQC Downstream Petroleum PCF v7.2.2, element 10252"@en ] ;
    dcterms:source [ a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
            dcterms:title "Step 3c definition workbook, approved row"@en ] ;
    skos:altLabel "Forecast Data Preparation"@en ;
    skos:broader proc:CM-1-1-1-1 ;
    skos:definition "Prepare and validate the reference data and demand history that each forecast cycle depends on — product and market hierarchies, customer and location groupings, units of measure, and the historical demand series cleansed of outliers and one-off distortions — so the statistical baseline is built from accurate, planning-consistent inputs."@en ;
    skos:inScheme mod:core ;
    skos:notation "CM 1.1.1.1.1" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Prepare Master Data To Create Demand Forecast"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote """Covers per-cycle readiness of forecasting inputs: maintaining forecast-specific reference data, aligning product and market hierarchies to planning definitions, and cleansing demand history for outliers, supply disruptions, and other events that would distort the baseline. Excludes supply-planning reference and parameter data, owned by Maintain Supply Planning Master Data (CM-1-1-2-12); excludes production-scheduling master data, owned by Maintain Production Scheduling Master Data (CM-1-1-7-2-1); excludes customer, price, product, tax, and location master data, owned by Manage Master Data under Order Management (CM-1-3-7-1); excludes enterprise master-data policy and governance, which sit with the Data Governance workstream.
In scope: Maintain forecast-specific reference data | align product and market hierarchies to planning definitions | cleanse and adjust demand history for distorting events | validate data readiness for the forecast cycle
Out of scope: Supply-planning master data (Maintain Supply Planning Master Data, CM-1-1-2-12) | production-scheduling master data (Maintain Production Scheduling Master Data, CM-1-1-7-2-1) | customer, price, product, tax, and location master data (Manage Master Data, CM-1-3-7-1) | enterprise master-data policy and governance (Data Governance workstream) | statistical model development (Develop Statistical Baseline, CM-1-1-1-1-2)"""@en ;
    intake:apqcDecision "REVIEW LINK"@en ;
    intake:conceptTypeCheck "process"@en ;
    intake:keyInputs "raw sales and lifting history | product and market hierarchy definitions | customer and location groupings | recorded demand-distorting events"@en ;
    intake:level "L5"@en ;
    intake:primaryOutput "validated forecasting dataset and reference data for the cycle"@en ;
    intake:primaryPurpose "Ensure each forecast cycle starts from validated reference data and cleansed demand history."@en ;
    intake:processHorizon "monthly"@en ;
    intake:referenceSources "SRC-EIA-GLOSS-001 | SRC-ASCM-CSCP-001"@en ;
    intake:relatedConcepts "precedes: Develop Statistical Baseline | enables: Produce Demand Forecast (CM-1-1-1-1)"@en ;
    intake:responsibleDomain "Commercial & Marketing"@en ;
    intake:terminologyNotes "Batch 03 (2026-09-19). Fourth of the four parallel master-data nodes; consolidation under a governed master-data capability is parked for the EPM Data Governance workstream per the decision recorded on CM-1-1-2-12 (2026-09-18) and deliberately not resolved here — the boundary to CM-1-1-2-12 was already established from its approved out_of_scope. APQC 10252 'Maintain master data' is a WEAK distribution-master-data candidate; comparative evidence only."@en .

proc:CM-1-1-1-1-2 a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:references [ a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
            dcterms:identifier "20043" ;
            dcterms:isPartOf src:apqc-pcf-7.2.2 ;
            dcterms:title "APQC Downstream Petroleum PCF v7.2.2, element 20043"@en ] ;
    dcterms:source [ a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
            dcterms:title "Step 3c definition workbook, approved row"@en ] ;
    skos:altLabel "Baseline Forecasting"@en,
        "Statistical Baseline Forecast"@en ;
    skos:broader proc:CM-1-1-1-1 ;
    skos:definition "Generate the objective statistical baseline forecast of product demand from cleansed history and demonstrated demand drivers, selecting and tuning forecasting methods by product and market segment before any judgmental input is applied."@en ;
    skos:inScheme mod:core ;
    skos:notation "CM 1.1.1.1.2" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Develop Statistical Baseline"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote """Covers producing the unbiased statistical starting point of the forecast cycle: choosing and parameterizing forecasting methods, generating the baseline at the agreed hierarchy levels, and documenting model fit and known limitations. The baseline is deliberately judgment-free — commercial knowledge enters in the adjustment step. Excludes adjusting the forecast with customer input and market intelligence, owned by Adjust Forecast Incorporating Customer Input and Market Intelligence (CM-1-1-1-1-3); excludes publication and disaggregation, owned by Publish Forecast and Generate Component Level Forecast Plan (CM-1-1-1-1-4); excludes measuring forecast performance, owned by Monitor Demand Forecasting Performance and Reporting (CM-1-1-1-1-5).
In scope: Select and tune statistical forecasting methods by segment | generate the baseline forecast at agreed hierarchy levels | apply demonstrated demand drivers | document model fit and limitations
Out of scope: Judgmental adjustment of the forecast (CM-1-1-1-1-3) | forecast publication and disaggregation (CM-1-1-1-1-4) | forecast performance measurement (CM-1-1-1-1-5) | trading revenue and asset forecasting (Forecasting & Optimization, CM-1-2-1-1)"""@en ;
    intake:apqcDecision "REJECTED"@en ;
    intake:conceptTypeCheck "process"@en ;
    intake:keyInputs "validated forecasting dataset | demand driver variables | historical model performance"@en ;
    intake:level "L5"@en ;
    intake:primaryOutput "statistical baseline forecast by product and market segment"@en ;
    intake:primaryPurpose "Produce the objective, judgment-free statistical starting point for the demand forecast."@en ;
    intake:processHorizon "monthly"@en ;
    intake:referenceSources "SRC-EIA-STEO-001 | SRC-IEA-OMR-001 | SRC-ASCM-CSCP-001"@en ;
    intake:relatedConcepts "follows: Prepare Master Data To Create Demand Forecast | precedes: Adjust Forecast Incorporating Customer Input and Market Intelligence"@en ;
    intake:responsibleDomain "Commercial & Marketing"@en ;
    intake:terminologyNotes "Batch 03 (2026-09-19). APQC 20043 'Develop baseline forecasts' scored STRONG but was REJECTED at the Step 3b human gate as circular validation (APQC validating APQC); authored independently per that rejection. Driver-based statistical modeling of fuels demand (economic activity, prices, weather) follows the practice documented in EIA STEO product-consumption modules; monthly product-level demand assessment follows IEA OMR practice. 'Baseline' is used in the demand-planning sense — the pre-judgment statistical forecast — not the plan-baseline sense used in backcasting."@en .

proc:CM-1-1-1-1-3 a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:references [ a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
            dcterms:identifier "10106" ;
            dcterms:isPartOf src:apqc-pcf-7.2.2 ;
            dcterms:title "APQC Downstream Petroleum PCF v7.2.2, element 10106"@en ] ;
    dcterms:source [ a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
            dcterms:title "Step 3c definition workbook, approved row"@en ] ;
    skos:altLabel "Consensus Forecast Adjustment"@en,
        "Judgmental Forecast Adjustment"@en ;
    skos:broader proc:CM-1-1-1-1 ;
    skos:definition "Review and adjust the statistical baseline with demand knowledge the models cannot see — customer plans and commitments, sales and marketing input, and market and competitive intelligence — recording each adjustment and its rationale so the agreed forecast reflects the best available view of demand."@en ;
    skos:inScheme mod:core ;
    skos:notation "CM 1.1.1.1.3" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Adjust Forecast Incorporating Customer Input and Market Intelligence"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote """Covers the judgmental overlay and agreement step of the forecast cycle: gathering structured input from customer-facing and market-facing teams, challenging and applying adjustments to the baseline, and recording who changed what and why so performance monitoring can attribute accuracy effects. Excludes producing the statistical baseline itself (CM-1-1-1-1-2); excludes gathering market and customer intelligence as an ongoing capability — this step consumes intelligence, it does not own its production; excludes negotiating or committing the underlying customer volumes, owned by Order Management (CM-1-3-7) and sales.
In scope: Collect structured customer and market input | review and challenge the statistical baseline | apply and document adjustments with rationale | agree the adjusted forecast for publication
Out of scope: Statistical baseline generation (CM-1-1-1-1-2) | ownership of market and customer intelligence production | customer negotiation and order commitment (Order Management, CM-1-3-7) | publication of the agreed forecast (CM-1-1-1-1-4)"""@en ;
    intake:apqcDecision "REVIEW LINK"@en ;
    intake:conceptTypeCheck "process"@en ;
    intake:keyInputs "statistical baseline forecast | customer plans and commitments | sales and marketing input | market and competitive intelligence"@en ;
    intake:level "L5"@en ;
    intake:primaryOutput "agreed adjusted forecast with documented adjustment rationale"@en ;
    intake:primaryPurpose "Turn the statistical baseline into the agreed forecast by applying documented customer and market knowledge."@en ;
    intake:processHorizon "monthly"@en ;
    intake:referenceSources "SRC-IEA-OMR-001 | SRC-ASCM-CSCP-001"@en ;
    intake:relatedConcepts "follows: Develop Statistical Baseline | precedes: Publish Forecast and Generate Component Level Forecast Plan"@en ;
    intake:responsibleDomain "Commercial & Marketing"@en ;
    intake:terminologyNotes "Batch 03 (2026-09-19). Written as the consensus/enrichment step of standard demand-planning practice; the IEA OMR's monthly demand revisions on new market information are the reference pattern for judgment applied over a statistical basis. Adjustments are recorded with rationale specifically so CM-1-1-1-1-5 can measure whether they added accuracy — the adjustment record is part of the process, not an implementation detail. APQC 10106 'Perform customer and market intelligence analysis' is REVIEW LINK; it describes the intelligence capability this step consumes, not this step itself."@en .

proc:CM-1-1-1-1-4 a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:references [ a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
            dcterms:identifier "10306" ;
            dcterms:isPartOf src:apqc-pcf-7.2.2 ;
            dcterms:title "APQC Downstream Petroleum PCF v7.2.2, element 10306"@en ] ;
    dcterms:source [ a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
            dcterms:title "Step 3c definition workbook, approved row"@en ] ;
    skos:altLabel "Forecast Publication"@en,
        "Publish Demand Forecast"@en ;
    skos:broader proc:CM-1-1-1-1 ;
    skos:definition "Approve and publish the agreed demand forecast as the versioned planning basis, and translate it into the component-level forecast plan — the detailed breakdown by product grade or component, location, and period — that downstream planning processes consume."@en ;
    skos:inScheme mod:core ;
    skos:notation "CM 1.1.1.1.4" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Publish Forecast and Generate Component Level Forecast Plan"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote """Covers the release step of the forecast cycle: final approval, version identification, disaggregation of the agreed forecast to the component level used by planning, and distribution to its consumers. The published version is the fixed reference that both planning and forecast-performance measurement run against. Excludes acting on the forecast — supply, production, inventory, and allocation decisions are owned by Regional Optimization (CM-1-1-2) and Refinery Planning (CM-1-1-4); excludes the consumers' own receipt and case-assembly steps, owned by Receive Demand Forecast (CM-1-2-1-1-2) and Capture Product Demand Requirements (CM-1-1-4-7-1).
In scope: Approve and version the forecast for release | disaggregate to the component-level forecast plan | distribute the published forecast to consuming processes | maintain the published version as the fixed reference for the period
Out of scope: Supply and allocation decisions (Regional Optimization, CM-1-1-2) | refinery case-basis assembly (Capture Product Demand Requirements, CM-1-1-4-7-1) | trading-side receipt (Receive Demand Forecast, CM-1-2-1-1-2) | forecast adjustment (CM-1-1-1-1-3)"""@en ;
    intake:apqcDecision "REJECTED"@en ;
    intake:conceptTypeCheck "process"@en ;
    intake:keyInputs "agreed adjusted forecast | product component and grade structures | planning calendar"@en ;
    intake:level "L5"@en ;
    intake:primaryOutput "published versioned demand forecast and component-level forecast plan"@en ;
    intake:primaryPurpose "Release one versioned, detailed demand forecast that all downstream planning consumes."@en ;
    intake:processHorizon "monthly"@en ;
    intake:referenceSources "SRC-EIA-STEO-001 | SRC-ORP-DPSC-001 | SRC-ASCM-CSCP-001"@en ;
    intake:relatedConcepts "follows: Adjust Forecast Incorporating Customer Input and Market Intelligence | precedes: Regional Optimization | enables: Capture Product Demand Requirements | enables: Receive Demand Forecast"@en ;
    intake:responsibleDomain "Commercial & Marketing"@en ;
    intake:terminologyNotes "Batch 03 (2026-09-19). 'Component level' is read as the detailed disaggregated planning level — product grade or blend component, location, and period — required by the consuming planning processes; the definition states the function without fixing a single technical reading. APQC 10306 'Generate line level plan' scored STRONG but was REJECTED at the Step 3b human gate as circular validation with an unrelated citation; authored independently. The published, versioned forecast is the contemporaneous baseline that CM-1-1-1-1-5 measures against — consistent with the locked backcasting discipline."@en .

proc:CM-1-1-1-1-5 a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:references [ a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
            dcterms:identifier "16574" ;
            dcterms:isPartOf src:apqc-pcf-7.2.2 ;
            dcterms:title "APQC Downstream Petroleum PCF v7.2.2, element 16574"@en ] ;
    dcterms:source [ a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
            dcterms:title "Step 3c definition workbook, approved row"@en ] ;
    skos:altLabel "Forecast Accuracy Monitoring"@en,
        "Forecast Performance Measurement"@en ;
    skos:broader proc:CM-1-1-1-1 ;
    skos:definition "Measure and report how well published demand forecasts predicted actual demand — tracking accuracy, bias, and the effect of adjustments at agreed levels and lags — and feed the findings back into forecasting methods and adjustment behavior."@en ;
    skos:inScheme mod:core ;
    skos:notation "CM 1.1.1.1.5" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Monitor Demand Forecasting Performance and Reporting"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote """Covers recurring forecast-performance measurement and reporting: comparing actual demand with the forecast as published for that period, analyzing error and bias by segment and lag, evaluating whether judgmental adjustments improved accuracy, reporting results, and recommending method and process improvements. Actuals are compared with the contemporaneously published forecast version, not a later revision. Excludes explaining supply-plan versus actual outcomes, owned by Regional Backcasting (CM-1-1-5) and Distribution Backcasting (CM-1-1-6); excludes agreeing the cross-functional forecasting process design with sales, owned by Develop & Agree Demand Forecasting Process (CM-1-3-5-1-2).
In scope: Compare actual demand with the published forecast version | analyze forecast error and bias by segment and lag | evaluate the accuracy effect of judgmental adjustments | report performance and recommend improvements
Out of scope: Plan-versus-actual supply and distribution variance analysis (Regional Backcasting, CM-1-1-5; Distribution Backcasting, CM-1-1-6) | forecasting process design and agreement (Develop & Agree Demand Forecasting Process, CM-1-3-5-1-2) | making the forecast adjustments themselves (CM-1-1-1-1-3)"""@en ;
    intake:apqcDecision "REVIEW LINK"@en ;
    intake:conceptTypeCheck "process"@en ;
    intake:keyInputs "published forecast versions | actual demand history | adjustment records with rationale"@en ;
    intake:level "L5"@en ;
    intake:primaryOutput "forecast performance report with improvement recommendations"@en ;
    intake:primaryPurpose "Establish whether published forecasts are getting more or less reliable, and why, so the forecasting cycle improves."@en ;
    intake:processHorizon "monthly"@en ;
    intake:referenceSources "SRC-EIA-STEO-001 | SRC-ASCM-CSCP-001"@en ;
    intake:relatedConcepts "follows: Publish Forecast and Generate Component Level Forecast Plan | uses-input: Adjust Forecast Incorporating Customer Input and Market Intelligence | enables: Produce Demand Forecast (CM-1-1-1-1)"@en ;
    intake:responsibleDomain "Commercial & Marketing"@en ;
    intake:terminologyNotes "Batch 03 (2026-09-19). Measures the forecast against actual demand using the as-published version as the fixed comparison basis — the same contemporaneous-baseline discipline locked for Regional and Distribution Backcasting, applied to the demand side. EIA's published STEO forecast-accuracy evaluations are the reference practice for measuring product-demand forecasts against realized data. Specific accuracy metrics and thresholds are deliberately not named; they belong to the KPI workstream, not the process definition. APQC 16574 'Monitor and report performance' is a WEAK marketing-channel candidate; comparative evidence only."@en .

proc:CM-1-1-2-1-1 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader proc:CM-1-1-2-1 ;
    skos:definition "Check notifications for new materials or locations; potential connection to NPR (New Product Realization) process"@en ;
    skos:inScheme mod:core ;
    skos:notation "CM 1.1.2.1.1" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Check if new location or material has been identified"@en ;
    intake:level "L5"@en .

proc:CM-1-1-2-1-2 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader proc:CM-1-1-2-1 ;
    skos:definition "Check if new location and / or material is included in XPIMS model"@en ;
    skos:inScheme mod:core ;
    skos:notation "CM 1.1.2.1.2" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Perform validation check for new location and material in XPIMS model"@en ;
    intake:level "L5"@en .

proc:CM-1-1-2-1-3 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader proc:CM-1-1-2-1 ;
    skos:definition "Update XPIMS model with new products (including pricing) and new location node, if needed"@en ;
    skos:inScheme mod:core ;
    skos:notation "CM 1.1.2.1.3" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Update XPIMS model with new products and new location node"@en ;
    intake:level "L5"@en .

proc:CM-1-1-2-1-4 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader proc:CM-1-1-2-1 ;
    skos:definition "Cross validate XPIMS products and location nodes with DPO products and location nodes"@en ;
    skos:inScheme mod:core ;
    skos:notation "CM 1.1.2.1.4" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Perform validation check for new location and material in DPO model"@en ;
    intake:level "L5"@en .

proc:CM-1-1-2-1-5 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader proc:CM-1-1-2-1 ;
    skos:definition "Update DPO model with new products and/or nodes"@en ;
    skos:inScheme mod:core ;
    skos:notation "CM 1.1.2.1.5" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Update DPO model with new products and/or nodes"@en ;
    intake:level "L5"@en .

proc:CM-1-1-2-1-6 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader proc:CM-1-1-2-1 ;
    skos:definition "Update PPIMS model with New Products"@en ;
    skos:inScheme mod:core ;
    skos:notation "CM 1.1.2.1.6" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Update PPIMS model with New Products"@en ;
    intake:level "L5"@en .

proc:CM-1-1-2-1-7 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader proc:CM-1-1-2-1 ;
    skos:definition "Develop price tags in MPR for each new location and / or material"@en ;
    skos:inScheme mod:core ;
    skos:notation "CM 1.1.2.1.7" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Create price tags for new location / material"@en ;
    intake:level "L5"@en .

proc:CM-1-1-2-1-8 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader proc:CM-1-1-2-1 ;
    skos:definition "Update location and product tag mapping in Profisee for master tags"@en ;
    skos:inScheme mod:core ;
    skos:notation "CM 1.1.2.1.8" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Update location and product tag mapping"@en ;
    intake:level "L5"@en .

proc:CM-1-1-2-10 a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:references [ a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
            dcterms:identifier "20688" ;
            dcterms:isPartOf src:apqc-pcf-7.2.2 ;
            dcterms:title "APQC Downstream Petroleum PCF v7.2.2, element 20688"@en ] ;
    dcterms:source [ a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
            dcterms:title "Step 3c definition workbook, approved row"@en ] ;
    skos:altLabel "Crude & Feedstock Allocation"@en,
        "Crude Allocation"@en,
        "Feedstock Allocation"@en ;
    skos:broader proc:CM-1-1-2 ;
    skos:definition "Assign available crude and feedstock cargoes, grades, and volumes to specific refineries and receipt windows so each site's approved production plan can be met at the best delivered economics across the region."@en ;
    skos:inScheme mod:core ;
    skos:notation "CM 1.1.2.10" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Crude Allocation Decision"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote """Covers the recurring allocation of secured or available crude and feedstock supply across competing refinery destinations, including grade-to-site matching, volume splits, timing of receipt windows, and reallocation when supply or plan assumptions change. Excludes crude purchase, negotiation, and trade execution, owned by Supply And Trading; excludes vessel, pipeline, and terminal movement execution, owned by Midstream; excludes the refinery's internal decision on which tanks and units process an allocated grade, owned by Refining.
In scope: Grade-to-refinery assignment | volume split across sites | receipt-window timing | reallocation on supply disruption or plan change | allocation of term and spot volumes against planned refinery slates
Out of scope: Crude purchasing and trade execution (Supply And Trading) | physical movement, berth and pipeline scheduling (Midstream) | unit-level crude processing decisions (Refining) | refinery slate economics selection (Refinery Planning)"""@en ;
    intake:apqcDecision "NO CANDIDATE"@en ;
    intake:conceptTypeCheck "process"@en ;
    intake:keyInputs "approved refinery production plan | secured and available crude supply position | crude and feedstock quality assays | delivered-cost and freight economics | refinery receipt and storage constraints"@en ;
    intake:level "L4"@en ;
    intake:parkedChildren "Allocate Term Crude Volumes | Allocate Spot Crude Volumes | Reallocate Crude on Supply Disruption"@en ;
    intake:primaryOutput "approved crude and feedstock allocation to refineries and receipt windows"@en ;
    intake:primaryPurpose "Decide which refinery receives which crude and feedstock volumes, and when, so the regional plan is met at best delivered economics."@en ;
    intake:processHorizon "monthly"@en ;
    intake:referenceSources "SRC-CMU-REFPLAN-001 | SRC-SNF-REFPS-001 | SRC-EIA-GLOSS-001"@en ;
    intake:relatedConcepts "informed-by: Refinery Planning | constrained-by: Inventory Management (CM-1-1-3-7) | precedes: Refinery Scheduling"@en ;
    intake:responsibleDomain "Commercial & Marketing"@en ;
    intake:terminologyNotes "Label retains the existing “Decision” suffix, but the concept is authored as the recurring allocation process, not the decision record or its output. A later naming pass should consider “Allocate Crude & Feedstock” for verb consistency with sibling labels; not changed in this batch. The boundary against Supply And Trading follows the locked SCM/Commercial rule: this concept places already-secured supply and does not choose counterparty, price, or contract."@en .

proc:CM-1-1-2-11 a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:references [ a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
            dcterms:identifier "16820" ;
            dcterms:isPartOf src:apqc-pcf-7.2.2 ;
            dcterms:title "APQC Downstream Petroleum PCF v7.2.2, element 16820"@en ] ;
    dcterms:source [ a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
            dcterms:title "Step 3c definition workbook, approved row"@en ] ;
    skos:altLabel "Finished Product Allocation"@en,
        "Product Allocation"@en,
        "Supply Allocation"@en ;
    skos:broader proc:CM-1-1-2 ;
    skos:definition "Assign available finished-product supply to markets, channels, terminals, and customer commitments for a planning period, so limited or constrained volumes are placed where they best serve contractual obligations and regional margin."@en ;
    skos:inScheme mod:core ;
    skos:notation "CM 1.1.2.11" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Product Allocation Decision"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote """Covers plan-level placement of finished product across markets, channels, and supply points, including the commercial priority rules applied when available supply cannot meet all demand, and reallocation when supply, demand, or logistics change. Excludes order-level allocation and release against an individual customer order, owned by Order Management; excludes rack and terminal loading allocation enforcement, owned by Terminal Loading; excludes physical movement and delivery execution, owned by Midstream and Distribution.
In scope: Market and channel volume placement | supply-point-to-demand-point assignment | commercial priority rules under constrained supply | exchange and third-party placement within the plan | reallocation on plan change
Out of scope: Order-level allocation and release (Allocate & Release Order, Order Management) | rack and terminal allocation enforcement (Manage Allocation, Terminal Loading) | sales-target setting (Determine & Allocate Sales Targets, Marketing) | pricing and offer construction (Commercial & Marketing pricing processes) | physical delivery (Midstream, Distribution)"""@en ;
    intake:apqcDecision "NO CANDIDATE"@en ;
    intake:conceptTypeCheck "process"@en ;
    intake:keyInputs "demand forecast | available and planned production | inventory position | contractual and regulatory supply obligations | logistics and terminal capacity | netback and margin economics"@en ;
    intake:level "L4"@en ;
    intake:parkedChildren "Define Product Allocation Priority Rules | Allocate Constrained Product Supply | Allocate Exchange & Third-Party Volumes"@en ;
    intake:primaryOutput "approved finished-product allocation plan by market, channel, and supply point"@en ;
    intake:primaryPurpose "Decide where available finished product is placed across markets, channels, and supply points to protect commitments and regional margin."@en ;
    intake:processHorizon "monthly"@en ;
    intake:referenceSources "SRC-ASCM-CSCP-001 | SRC-SNF-REFPS-001 | SRC-EIA-GLOSS-001"@en ;
    intake:relatedConcepts "informed-by: Produce Demand Forecast (CM-1-1-1-1) | constrained-by: Inventory Management (CM-1-1-3-7) | enables: Order Management | enables: Terminal Loading"@en ;
    intake:responsibleDomain "Commercial & Marketing"@en ;
    intake:terminologyNotes "Three allocation concepts coexist at different grains and are deliberately bounded here: plan-level placement (this node), order-level allocation and release (Order Management), and loading-time allocation enforcement (Terminal Loading). The “Decision” suffix is retained pending the same naming pass noted on CM-1-1-2-10."@en .

proc:CM-1-1-2-12 a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:references [ a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
            dcterms:identifier "10252" ;
            dcterms:isPartOf src:apqc-pcf-7.2.2 ;
            dcterms:title "APQC Downstream Petroleum PCF v7.2.2, element 10252"@en ] ;
    dcterms:source [ a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
            dcterms:title "Step 3c definition workbook, approved row"@en ] ;
    skos:altLabel "Planning Parameter Maintenance"@en,
        "Supply Planning Reference Data Maintenance"@en ;
    skos:broader proc:CM-1-1-2 ;
    skos:definition "Create, maintain, and retire the reference and parameter data that the regional supply-planning model depends on — such as planning network, sourcing, capacity, lead-time, yield, and product-grouping data — so planning results remain accurate and reproducible."@en ;
    skos:inScheme mod:core ;
    skos:notation "CM 1.1.2.12" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Maintain Supply Planning Master Data"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote """Covers stewardship of supply-planning-specific reference and parameter data over its lifecycle, including requesting and validating changes, applying effective dates, and confirming that planning results remain consistent after a change. Excludes enterprise master-data policy, standards, and governance, which sit with the Data Governance workstream; excludes customer, price, product, tax, and location master data, owned by Manage Master Data under Order Management; excludes production-scheduling master data, owned by Maintain Production Scheduling Master Data under Refinery Scheduling.
In scope: Planning network and location data | sourcing and supply-path data | planning capacity and rate parameters | lead times and transit assumptions | planning yields and product groupings | change request, validation, and effective dating of planning parameters
Out of scope: Enterprise master-data policy and governance standards (Data Governance) | customer, price, product, tax, and location master data (Manage Master Data, Order Management) | production-scheduling master data (Maintain Production Scheduling Master Data, Refinery Scheduling) | demand-forecast master data preparation (Prepare Master Data To Create Demand Forecast, Produce Demand Forecast (CM-1-1-1-1)) | planning application administration and platform support (Process Excellence & IT)"""@en ;
    intake:apqcDecision "NO SOURCE"@en ;
    intake:conceptTypeCheck "process"@en ;
    intake:keyInputs "planning parameter change requests | network, capacity, and sourcing changes | refinery and logistics capability updates | product and grade structure changes | enterprise data-governance standards"@en ;
    intake:level "L4"@en ;
    intake:parkedChildren "Maintain Planning Network Data | Maintain Planning Capacity & Rate Parameters | Maintain Planning Yield Data"@en ;
    intake:primaryOutput "validated and effective-dated supply-planning reference and parameter data"@en ;
    intake:primaryPurpose "Keep the reference and parameter data behind regional supply planning accurate, current, and reproducible."@en ;
    intake:processHorizon "periodic"@en ;
    intake:referenceSources "SRC-ASCM-CSCP-001"@en ;
    intake:relatedConcepts "enables: Regional Optimization | governed-by: Data Governance | informed-by: Refinery Planning"@en ;
    intake:responsibleDomain "Commercial & Marketing"@en ;
    intake:terminologyNotes "Defined narrowly per Hamid's decision (2026-09-18, Option 1): scope is the supply-planning-specific reference and parameter data consumed by the regional planning model, not master data generally. The taxonomy currently carries four parallel master-data nodes — this one, Maintain Production Scheduling Master Data (CM-1-1-7-2-1), Manage Master Data (CM-1-3-7-1), and Prepare Master Data To Create Demand Forecast (CM-1-1-1-1-1). Their consolidation, and whether a single governed master-data capability should own them, is parked for the EPM Data Governance workstream and is deliberately not resolved here. APQC candidate “Maintain master data” was triaged STRONG but accepted by no validator; used as comparative evidence only, not adopted."@en .

proc:CM-1-1-2-13 a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:references [ a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
            dcterms:identifier "10359" ;
            dcterms:isPartOf src:apqc-pcf-7.2.2 ;
            dcterms:title "APQC Downstream Petroleum PCF v7.2.2, element 10359"@en ] ;
    dcterms:source [ a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
            dcterms:title "Step 3c definition workbook, approved row"@en ] ;
    skos:altLabel "Finished Goods Inventory Planning"@en,
        "Finished Product Inventory Planning"@en ;
    skos:broader proc:CM-1-1-2 ;
    skos:definition "Set and optimize the planned finished-product inventory levels and positions for the regional plan period, balancing supply availability, demand coverage, and working-capital cost within established inventory policy and storage constraints."@en ;
    skos:inScheme mod:core ;
    skos:notation "CM 1.1.2.13" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Plan Finished Goods Inventory"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote """Covers the planning decision on how much finished product should be held, in which grades, and at which supply points and terminals across the regional plan horizon, including target and minimum operating positions, seasonal and pre-build positions, and the inventory consequences of allocation and production choices. Excludes the setting of inventory policy itself, and excludes inventory measurement, reconciliation, replenishment, consignment, commingled, and re-brand inventory management, all owned by the Inventory Management cluster under Distribution Planning & Scheduling. Excludes physical storage operation, owned by Midstream.
In scope: Planned finished-product inventory targets by grade and location | minimum operating and safety positions within policy | seasonal and pre-build inventory positioning | inventory implications of allocation and production plan choices | working-capital and storage-cost trade-offs in the plan
Out of scope: Finished-product inventory policy setting (Develop Finished Product Inventory Policy, Inventory Management) | inventory measurement and reconciliation (Inventory Management) | replenishment execution (Manage Inventory Replenishment, Inventory Management) | consignment, commingled, lot/batch, and re-brand inventory management (Inventory Management) | physical tank and terminal storage operation (Midstream)"""@en ;
    intake:apqcDecision "NO SOURCE"@en ;
    intake:conceptTypeCheck "process"@en ;
    intake:keyInputs "demand forecast | planned production and supply availability | approved inventory policy | storage and terminal capacity | product specifications and seasonal grade changes | working-capital and storage-cost assumptions"@en ;
    intake:level "L4"@en ;
    intake:parkedChildren "Set Regional Inventory Targets | Plan Seasonal Inventory Build | Plan Inventory for Constrained Supply"@en ;
    intake:primaryOutput "approved planned finished-product inventory targets and positions for the plan period"@en ;
    intake:primaryPurpose "Decide how much finished product should be held, in which grades, and where, across the regional plan horizon."@en ;
    intake:processHorizon "monthly"@en ;
    intake:referenceSources "SRC-ASCM-CSCP-001 | SRC-SNF-REFPS-001"@en ;
    intake:relatedConcepts "constrained-by: Inventory Management (CM-1-1-3-7) | informed-by: Produce Demand Forecast (CM-1-1-1-1) | informed-by: Refinery Planning | enables: Product Allocation Decision"@en ;
    intake:responsibleDomain "Commercial & Marketing"@en ;
    intake:terminologyNotes "Boundary resolved per Hamid's decision (2026-09-18, Option 1): this node owns the planned inventory level and position inside the regional plan, while the Inventory Management cluster under Distribution Planning & Scheduling (CM-1-1-3-7) retains policy, measurement, reconciliation, and replenishment. This preserves both approved scope notes — Regional Optimization explicitly names “inventory positioning” — and the locked SCM rule, by separating the plan-period target decision from ongoing inventory management. No tree change required. “Finished goods” retained from the existing label although “finished product” is the more common downstream term; alt labels carry both."@en .

