    skos:definition "Formulate alternative strategic models for delivering the consumer value proposition — fuel-led, convenience-led, loyalty-led, digital-led, and mixed models — and evaluate them against the proposition objectives and the governed evidence base."@en ;
    skos:inScheme mod:core ;
    skos:notation "CM 1.3.2.3.2" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Formulate and Evaluate Strategic Operating Alternatives (CVP)"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote """Covers alternative formulation and evaluation for the consumer proposition: defining candidate delivery models; evaluating against principles and objectives, consumer findings, retail economics, and brand direction; recommending the preferred alternative to the develop/update step (CM-1-3-2-3-4). Excludes proposition strategy development and approval (CM-1-3-2-3-4); retail network design (CM-1-3-3-4); offer definition (CM-1-3-3-1).
In scope: Define candidate consumer-proposition delivery models | evaluate against objectives, evidence, and economics | recommend with evidence
Out of scope: Proposition strategy development and approval (CM-1-3-2-3-4) | retail network design (CM-1-3-3-4) | offer definition (CM-1-3-3-1)"""@en ;
    intake:apqcDecision "REVIEW LINK"@en ;
    intake:conceptTypeCheck "process"@en ;
    intake:keyInputs "Principles and objectives (CM-1-3-2-3-3) | consumer findings (CM-1-3-1-3) | retail economics"@en ;
    intake:level "L5"@en ;
    intake:primaryOutput "Evaluated consumer-proposition delivery alternatives with a recommendation"@en ;
    intake:primaryPurpose "The consumer promise delivered the best way, chosen from real alternatives."@en ;
    intake:processHorizon "strategic"@en ;
    intake:referenceSources "SRC-APQC-PCF-001"@en ;
    intake:relatedConcepts "follows: Establish CVP principles and objectives | precedes: Test Customer value proposition | governed-by: Consumer Value Proposition"@en ;
    intake:responsibleDomain "Commercial & Marketing"@en ;
