proc:CM-1-3-6-8 a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:references [ a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
            dcterms:identifier "17467" ;
            dcterms:isPartOf src:apqc-pcf-7.2.2 ;
            dcterms:title "APQC Downstream Petroleum PCF v7.2.2, element 17467"@en ] ;
    dcterms:source [ a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
            dcterms:title "Step 3c definition workbook, approved row"@en ] ;
    skos:altLabel "Commercial Agreement Compliance Management"@en ;
    skos:broader proc:CM-1-3-6 ;
    skos:definition "Manage compliance with commercial obligations in branded sales-network agreements by planning and conducting agreement-based reviews, validating reported sales and other obligation inputs, reporting discrepancies, and routing findings to the accountable relationship, Finance, O2C, Legal, and compliance owners for resolution."@en ;
    skos:inScheme mod:core ;
    skos:notation "CM 1.3.6.8" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Compliance Management"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote """Narrow-scope statement: Applies only to contractual/commercial obligations that partners, franchisees, dealers, licensees, marketers, or other network participants report under executed agreements — for example sales-based royalties, brand fees, rebates, promotional-fund contributions, volume commitments, reporting duties, and agreed standards evidence where audit rights exist. Reviews cover only obligations that are defined in an executed agreement, subject to review/audit rights, within a valid review period, and supported by agreed record-access rights. Enterprise regulatory compliance (fuels, environmental, safety, trade), corporate Internal Audit, financial-statement audit, and tax audit remain with their accountable functions. Findings route to their owners: financial adjustments and collections through the accountable Finance/O2C processes, including Manage Collection of Royalty and Fees; enforcement under agreements through relationship management and Legal. Fact-dependent statement: where a remedy would affect a franchise relationship governed by the Petroleum Marketing Practices Act, the determination is reserved to Legal.
In scope: Agreement-based compliance review planning within audit rights and review periods | validation of reported sales and other obligation inputs | discrepancy reporting | findings routing to accountable relationship, Finance, O2C, Legal, and compliance owners | compliance status reporting
Out of scope: Regulatory compliance programs (EHS, fuels, trade — their functions) | Internal Audit, financial-statement audit, and tax audit | collections and financial adjustment execution (Finance/O2C) | enforcement remedies (relationship management; Legal) | obligations outside executed agreements or valid review periods"""@en ;
    intake:apqcDecision "REVIEW LINK"@en ;
    intake:conceptTypeCheck "process"@en ;
    intake:keyInputs "Executed agreements, audit rights, and review periods | reported sales and obligations data | royalty/fee/rebate bases"@en ;
    intake:level "L4"@en ;
    intake:primaryOutput "Validated commercial compliance with routed findings"@en ;
    intake:primaryPurpose "Commercial obligations across the network verifiably reported and settled on an accurate basis."@en ;
    intake:processHorizon "periodic"@en ;
    intake:referenceSources "SRC-APQC-PCF-001; SRC-PMPA-001"@en ;
    intake:relatedConcepts "enables: Manage Collection of Royalty and Fees | informed-by: Report Franchise Performance"@en ;
    intake:responsibleDomain "Commercial & Marketing"@en ;
    intake:terminologyNotes "Batch 30 (2026-09-20). Review canonical definition, narrow-scope statement, and agreement-rights conditions adopted verbatim — commercial-agreement compliance only, never an enterprise compliance catch-all. Preferred label 'Commercial Agreement Compliance Management' recorded as alt label and queued as the priority rename: it encodes the approved narrow scope."@en .

